Subject: [PATCH] setupapi: make SPDRP_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_OBJECT_NAME readable

The PropertyMap entry for SPDRP_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_OBJECT_NAME is a NULL
placeholder, so every SetupDiGetDeviceRegistryProperty() asking for it fails.

It is not a decorative property. An application that wants to know which drive
letter belongs to which device joins this string against QueryDosDevice(), and
with the property unavailable the join can never succeed -- the device is
enumerated but can never be matched to a volume.

Measured with rekordbox 7.2.18: its USB export browser enumerates
GUID_DEVCLASS_VOLUME, reads SPDRP_CAPABILITIES, SPDRP_DEVICEDESC,
SPDRP_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_OBJECT_NAME and SPDRP_FRIENDLYNAME from each device, then
walks the drive letters and matches on

    SPDRP_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_OBJECT_NAME == QueryDosDeviceW(letter)

which on this machine is "\Device\Harddisk1" for E:. With the property mapped to
a registry value the match succeeds and the device appears.

Backing it with a registry value is the smallest change that makes the read work
and lets whoever creates the devnode supply the name.

---
--- a/dlls/setupapi/devinst.c
+++ b/dlls/setupapi/devinst.c
@@ -605,7 +605,21 @@
     PROPERTY_MAP_ENTRY(REG_SZ, "Mfg", DEVPROP_TYPE_STRING),
     PROPERTY_MAP_ENTRY(REG_SZ, "FriendlyName", 0),
     PROPERTY_MAP_ENTRY(REG_SZ, "LocationInformation", DEVPROP_TYPE_STRING),
-    { 0, NULL, NULL, DEVPROP_TYPE_STRING }, /* SPDRP_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_OBJECT_NAME */
+    /* RBW-PDONAME: SPDRP_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_OBJECT_NAME was a NULL placeholder, so
+     * every SetupDiGetDeviceRegistryProperty() asking for it failed. It is not a
+     * decorative property: an application that wants to know which drive letter
+     * belongs to which device joins this string against QueryDosDevice(), and
+     * with the property unavailable the join can never succeed.
+     *
+     * Measured with rekordbox 7.2.18: its EXPORT-mode device browser enumerates
+     * GUID_DEVCLASS_VOLUME, reads SPDRP_CAPABILITIES, SPDRP_DEVICEDESC,
+     * SPDRP_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_OBJECT_NAME and SPDRP_FRIENDLYNAME from each device,
+     * and then matches that third one against QueryDosDeviceW(L"E:") --
+     * "\\Device\\Harddisk1" here.
+     *
+     * Backing it with a registry value lets whoever creates the devnode supply
+     * it, and makes the read succeed instead of failing outright. */
+    PROPERTY_MAP_ENTRY(REG_SZ, "PhysicalDeviceObjectName", DEVPROP_TYPE_STRING), /* SPDRP_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_OBJECT_NAME */
     PROPERTY_MAP_ENTRY(REG_DWORD, "Capabilities", DEVPROP_TYPE_INT32),
     PROPERTY_MAP_ENTRY(REG_DWORD, "UINumber", DEVPROP_TYPE_INT32),
     PROPERTY_MAP_ENTRY(REG_MULTI_SZ, "UpperFilters", DEVPROP_TYPE_STRING_LIST),
